// U7 Pretest

::U7 Pretest Q01::What does “trace a claim” require? {=Locate the original study, data, or statement and inspect its context.~Read only summaries that repeat the claim.~Count social-media likes.~Ask whether the headline is memorable.}

::U7 Pretest Q02::What is the best conclusion when evidence is mixed and limited? {=State uncertainty and avoid a stronger claim than the evidence supports.~Choose the most exciting result.~Treat uncertainty as proof of harm.~Ignore all evidence.}

::U7 Pretest Q03::Neighborhood B has a higher asthma-visit rate and more traffic. What may be concluded? {=There is a pattern worth investigating, but the data alone do not prove traffic caused it.~Traffic definitely caused every visit.~The neighborhoods are identical.~Rates cannot be compared.}

::U7 Pretest Q04::What best distinguishes correlation from causation? {=Correlation shows variables move together; causation requires evidence that one produces change in the other.~Correlation is stronger than experimental evidence.~They mean exactly the same thing.~Causation requires no mechanism.}

::U7 Pretest Q05::Which call to action is most usable? {=Refill your bottle at the station beside the library entrance today.~Care more about hydration.~Make better choices someday.~Everyone should change.}

::U7 Pretest Q06::Which message avoids stigmatizing framing? {=Describe the barrier and available support without blaming affected people.~Label people by a health condition.~Use fear and shame to force action.~Assume behavior reflects character.}

::U7 Pretest Q07::Which goal is SMART? {=For four weeks, average 7.5 hours of sleep on school nights using a nightly log.~Sleep more eventually.~Become perfectly healthy.~Never feel tired again.}

::U7 Pretest Q08::Why consider nine wellness domains? {=Domains interact, so a plan should anticipate benefits and tradeoffs.~Every domain must receive identical time.~Only physical wellness can be measured.~Domains never affect one another.}

::U7 Pretest Q09::What should remain continuous across a transition? {=Core purpose and effective protective factors, when still relevant.~Every exact action regardless of circumstances.~Every baseline value.~All barriers.}

::U7 Pretest Q10::What makes a wellness strategy sustainable? {=It fits available resources, can be monitored, and can adapt over time.~It requires maximum effort every day.~It depends on one unavailable resource.~It has no review process.}
